      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not easily. The indentation makes it impossible with a std::ostream. Consider a vector\u003cHowTargetContainsFile\u003e as an example\n\nWe currently write:\n```\n[\n  Pair(\n    Target //path/to:target,\n    Enum value 2\n  )\n]\n```\n\nIn order to indent correctly, we would need to either not use a standard ostream, or pass it around as additional context. Both would break the PrintTo interface.\n\nIMO this isn\u0027t too much of an issue because if you want to interop with a value that defines PrintTo, you can just create a pretty method that creates a string stream and calls `PrintTo` on it, returning the buffer it wrote to.",
